==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|sco|pernickety}}, {{m|sco|persnickety}}, of uncertain origin; the ''Dictionary of the Scots Language'' says that it resembles {{m|sco|per-||intensifying prefix}} + {{m|sco|nick}}, but might be derived from ''particular'' + ''finicky'' with the form influenced by past participles ending in ''-et'', ''-it'', ''-ed''.<ref>{{R:DSL|pernicketie}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|British}} {{IPA|en|/pɜː(ɹ)ˈnɪk.ɪ.ti/|/pɜː(ɹ)ˈnɪk.ə.ti/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪkɪti}} ''or'' {{rhymes|en|ɪkəti}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|British}} [[fussy|Fussy]]; paying [[undue]] [[attention]] to [[minor]] [[detail]]s; [[fastidious]].
# Requiring attention to minor details.

====Synonyms====
* [[niggly]]
* [[persnickety]] {{qualifier|US}}; more on [[Thesaurus:fastidious]]

